date-released: 2026-11-04
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23944243"  # concept DOI, resolves to the latest version
abstract: >-
  adaptdg is a Python library for adaptive stabilised discontinuous-Galerkin (DG) transport and PDE solvers on FEniCSx
  (DOLFINx 0.11). It discretises advection-diffusion-reaction problems with DG and minimises the residual in a dual DG
  norm, which gives a stable solution and an error indicator that drives adaptive mesh refinement (Dörfler marking).
  It includes a variational multiscale (VMS) reconstruction for stationary and unsteady problems (backward Euler and
  BDF2) in 2D and 3D, with linear and nonlinear (Burgers) cases; 1D and 2D transient transport with conservative
  mesh-to-mesh transfer; and drivers for two reactive-transport benchmarks, where the chemistry enters through callbacks
  and adaptdg itself contains no chemistry. It is an updated implementation of the method of Giraldo and Calo (2023,
  Computer Methods in Applied Mechanics and Engineering 417:116285, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cma.2023.116285), which is
  its reference; the examples in examples/vms follow the settings of the published figures. Successor of AS-FEM.
